cgroup-v1: let CAP_SYS_NICE move other users' tasks, as Android's kernels do

Khadas Edge1, Android 14 on mainline 6.12. Applied to kernel/mainline by
build/build-kernel.sh before every build (device/khadas/edge/kernel/patches/).

Android keeps every app process in a cpuset, cpu and blkio group chosen by its
state (top-app, foreground, background ...), and system_server moves them there:
uid system, with CAP_SYS_NICE, writing to cgroup.procs and tasks files that init
has made system-owned. Mainline's cgroup v1 lets a writer move only its own tasks
unless it is root, so every move of an app failed:

  E libprocessgroup: AddTidToCgroup failed to write '501'; path=foreground;
    process: Permission denied

- 700 times on card 14, and no app left the root group. Android's common kernels
carry the same exception for CAP_SYS_NICE. Checked against the opener's
credentials (file_ns_capable), like the uid test it extends, so an inherited fd
grants nothing its opener did not have.

diff --git a/kernel/cgroup/cgroup-v1.c b/kernel/cgroup/cgroup-v1.c
index e28d5f0d2..e55b9a800 100644
--- a/kernel/cgroup/cgroup-v1.c
+++ b/kernel/cgroup/cgroup-v1.c
@@ -517,9 +517,18 @@ static ssize_t __cgroup1_procs_write(struct kernfs_open_file *of,
 	 */
 	cred = of->file->f_cred;
 	tcred = get_task_cred(task);
+	/*
+	 * Android: system_server moves every app's processes between the cpuset,
+	 * cpu and blkio groups (task_profiles.json), as uid system and with
+	 * CAP_SYS_NICE. Android's common kernels let CAP_SYS_NICE do that; without
+	 * it each move fails with EACCES ("AddTidToCgroup failed to write ...
+	 * Permission denied") and no app ever leaves the root group. The
+	 * capability is the opener's, like the uid above.
+	 */
 	if (!uid_eq(cred->euid, GLOBAL_ROOT_UID) &&
 	    !uid_eq(cred->euid, tcred->uid) &&
-	    !uid_eq(cred->euid, tcred->suid))
+	    !uid_eq(cred->euid, tcred->suid) &&
+	    !file_ns_capable(of->file, &init_user_ns, CAP_SYS_NICE))
 		ret = -EACCES;
 	put_cred(tcred);
 	if (ret)
